// Continental Europe-Maghreb: the Continental European synchronous area with the
// Maghreb systems that run in step with it (spec section 28.3; research note
// docs/research/2026-10-18-world-power-grids-top-8.md, section "B -
// Continental Europe-Maghreb"): the continent from Portugal to Turkiye with
// western Denmark (DK1), connected Ukraine and Moldova, the Baltic states,
// Sicily, Malta and Crete, and Morocco, northern interconnected Algeria and
// Tunisia through the Spain-Morocco AC link. The notes exclude the Nordic
// area, eastern Denmark (DK2), Great Britain, Ireland, Sardinia, Corsica,
// separately operated islands and isolated southern Algeria; ENTSO-E
// membership alone is not the boundary.
//
// Grid-operation rulings:
// - DK1 is in and DK2 is out: Natural Earth admin-0 DNK less the 1:10m
//   admin-1 regions Hovedstaden (with Bornholm) and Sjaelland (Zealand,
//   Lolland-Falster), so Nordjylland, Midtjylland and Syddanmark (Jutland and
//   Funen) remain.
// - Out as separately operated systems: Sardinia (the eight 1:10m admin-1
//   provinces), Corsica (Haute-Corse and Corse-du-Sud), the Balearics
//   (Baleares) and the Canaries (Las Palmas and Santa Cruz de Tenerife).
//   Cyprus, Great Britain, Ireland, the Nordic countries, Russia and Belarus
//   are not selected. The smaller non-interconnected Aegean islands (Lesbos,
//   Rhodes, Chios and the like) fall under the extractor's 2-cell land floor.
// - Crimea and Sevastopol are out (spec section 28.3, user decision
//   2026-10-25). Natural Earth's 1:50m admin-0 UKR already leaves Crimea to
//   RUS (checked: neither Simferopol nor Sevastopol lies in UKR's polygons),
//   and the canonical extent (crates/infrastructure/authoring/
//   ukraine_ips_operating_extent.ron) is pasted verbatim as an exclusion
//   (ruling 11). Mainland Ukraine, Donetsk and Luhansk included, is in.
// - Isolated southern Algeria is out, with a schematic boundary at 30 N: the
//   In Salah-Adrar-Timimoun pole (PIAT) is a separate southern system that a
//   planned double 400 kV Hassi R'mel-Timimoun line would join to the
//   national interconnected network (RIN), and a Ghardaia-Tamanrasset line is
//   only under consideration (Enerdata, "Sonelgaz launches a 700 km
//   transmission project to link Algeria's power grids", 2023-05-04). The
//   exclusion is 1:10m admin-1 Adrar, Tamanghasset, Tindouf, Bechar, Ouargla,
//   Illizi and Ghardaia south of 30 N.
// - Areas the notes don't address (spec section 28.3):
//   - Transnistria is in. Its Moldavskaya GRES supplied about 70% of
//     Moldova's electricity before Moldova's grid synchronised with
//     Continental Europe on 16 March 2022 (Moldova Ministry of Energy, "How
//     Has the Energy Sector Transformed with the Boost of Renewable Energy?",
//     2025-09-19, section "Synchronization with the Continental Grid Was a
//     Game-Changer", paragraphs 2-4). It lies inside admin-0 MDA.
//   - Kosovo is in (ADM0 KOS). KOSTT began operating as a regulatory zone
//     of the Continental European system, in the Kosovo-Albania block, when
//     its ENTSO-E connection agreement took effect on 14 December 2020
//     (KoSSev, "KOSTT starts operation as a regulatory zone within the
//     Kosovo-Albania bloc", 2020-12-14).
//   - Western Sahara is in from the Moroccan border south to Dakhla, west of
//     the berm, which Natural Earth's admin-0 MAR outline already contains.
//     Sourced ONEE grid operation:
//     - Laayoune: the 470 km Tiznit-Laayoune line (Le Matin, "Mise en service
//       d'une nouvelle ligne electrique Tres Haute Tension reliant Tiznit a
//       Laayoune", 2015-08-04). Laayoune joined the 225 kV national grid in
//       1998, which let Smara Province be connected in 2000 (FNH, "Entretien.
//       Les regions du Sud du Maroc beneficient d'un gisement en energies
//       renouvelables exceptionnel", interview with ONEE's Director General,
//       2021-09-01, first answer, first paragraph).
//     - Boujdour and the Aftissat wind farm at 400 kV since February 2018
//       (EcoActu, "Raccordement de Dakhla au reseau electrique: le DG de
//       l'ONEE s'enquiert de l'etat d'avancement des travaux", 2021-02-26).
//     - Dakhla: a 400 kV double-circuit line now reaches the city (Le360,
//       "Info360. Lancement imminent d'une nouvelle liaison electrique entre
//       Boujdour et Marrakech", 2025-11-03, paragraph beginning "A signaler
//       que le reseau").
//     The rest of the interior west of the berm is in by authoring judgment:
//     administrative extent west of the berm; only the coastal backbone
//     (Tiznit-Laayoune-Boujdour-Dakhla) and Smara Province are sourced.
//     Out: the part east of the berm (Natural Earth's separate ADM0 SAH
//     feature, not selected) and everything south of 23.55 N, a schematic
//     exclusion just south of Dakhla (23.70 N) listed after the generated
//     rings, where no source shows the grid.
//
// Geography: tools/region_authoring/selections/continental_europe_maghreb.args
// holds the extractor arguments: Natural Earth v5.1.2 1:50m admin-0 for 41
// countries (Kosovo by ADM0 KOS), dissolved (ruling 8), with the 1:10m
// admin-1 exclusions above. Regenerate with
//   tr '\n' '\0' < tools/region_authoring/selections/continental_europe_maghreb.args \
//       | xargs -0 python3 -I tools/region_authoring/natural_earth.py
// which reports 12 land and 22 exclude rings. The land rings are the
// mainland (Iberia to Ukraine and Thrace), Anatolia, the Maghreb, Sicily,
// Crete, Euboea, Funen, Saaremaa, and Zealand, Mallorca, Corsica and Sardinia
// (each under its exclusion). The selection's exclusions dissolve into 26
// rings, 23 of which meet the bounds; 22 come out (ruling 9). The one that
// collapses is a 4-point Haute-Corse islet (9.46-9.48 E, 42.62-42.65 N) that
// lies in no included land ring, so no land is re-admitted. The southern
// Algeria run (continental_europe_maghreb_algeria_south.args, extent mode)
// reports 1 exclude ring from 1 dissolved ring meeting its bounds.
// Tolerance: 0.02 degrees in both runs, the same as assets/regions/ips_ups.ron
// and the canonical Crimea extent, so the shared IPS/UPS borders (Ukraine,
// Moldova, the Baltic states, Poland and Turkiye against Russia, Belarus and
// Georgia) are the same 1:50m admin-0 lines simplified alike.
// IPS/UPS seam (ruling 10): the same borders are not enough, because a cell
// is playable when its centre is, and an IPS/UPS land cell (1.0 x 0.5
// degrees) reaches up to half a cell past the border. Ten IPS/UPS land cells
// held 14 Europe-Maghreb land centres, and one IPS/UPS centre fell in a
// Europe-Maghreb land cell, so those ten IPS/UPS cells are excluded here, after
// the generated rings; with them no centre is playable in both regions.
// Nudge rings after the generated land put coastal cities and starter plants
// whose cell centres fall offshore on land, and give Malta, Crete and Sicily
// a land cell at Valletta, Heraklion and Palermo. Schematic exclusions open
// the Strait of Messina and cut Western Sahara south of Dakhla. The grid's
// rows are placed so a row of centres lies in the Strait of Gibraltar, so
// the starter link crosses one water cell.
// Points are (lon, lat) in degrees.
//
// Grid: 16.65 W to 44.95 E and 22.87 to 59.87 N on 154 x 123 cells (0.4 x
// 0.3008 degrees). At the middle latitude, 41.37 N, a cell is 33.38 km
// east-west by 33.45 km north-south (aspect 1.002, cell_km 33.414).
//
// Money is in EUR at local price levels from the Plan 7 research note
// (docs/research/2026-10-25-plan-7-regional-economics.md), converted to game
// values by its pacing method. Each entry's comment cites its rows and shows
// the arithmetic; the ratios use full precision (ruling 25). The catalog is
// economic zone 0, the regional default, from the note's "Europe-Maghreb
// economic-zone proposal": German technology-level capital (P7-DE-001 to
// P7-DE-007, midpoints) with pan-European ERAA O&M and fuel. Spain (zone 1)
// and Morocco (zone 2) override wind and solar construction from whole
// projects (the economic_zones block). Countries on zone 0 by authoring
// choice (the note's "Regional default by authoring choice"): Portugal,
// France, Belgium, the Netherlands, Luxembourg, Germany, Switzerland, Austria,
// Italy (with Sicily), Malta, Slovenia, Croatia, Bosnia and Herzegovina,
// Serbia, Montenegro, North Macedonia, Albania, Greece (with Crete), Bulgaria,
// Romania, Hungary, Slovakia, Czechia, Poland, Lithuania, Latvia, Estonia,
// Denmark (DK1), Ukraine, Moldova (with Transnistria), Turkiye, northern
// Algeria, Tunisia, Kosovo, Andorra, Monaco, Liechtenstein, San Marino and
// Vatican City. Algeria and Tunisia have no whole-project row.
(
    region_schema: 4,
    id: "continental_europe_maghreb",
    system_zone: 2,
    // Civil clocks (spec section 28.4). The EU zones observe summer time from
    // April to October (most days of each month). Central European Time is the
    // dispatcher's clock; Morocco, Algeria and Tunisia keep UTC+1 all year
    // (Morocco's Ramadan shift is not modelled), and Turkiye keeps UTC+3.
    time_zones: [
        (id: 1, name_key: "zone-wet", standard_offset_minutes: 0, dst_months: [false, false, false, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, false, false]),
        (id: 2, name_key: "zone-cet", standard_offset_minutes: 60, dst_months: [false, false, false, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, false, false]),
        (id: 3, name_key: "zone-cet-fixed", standard_offset_minutes: 60, dst_months: [false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false]),
        (id: 4, name_key: "zone-eet", standard_offset_minutes: 120, dst_months: [false, false, false, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, false, false]),
        (id: 5, name_key: "zone-trt", standard_offset_minutes: 180, dst_months: [false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false]),
    ],
    // Northern meteorological seasons.
    calendar: (seasons: [Winter, Winter, Spring, Spring, Spring, Summer, Summer, Summer, Autumn, Autumn, Autumn, Winter]),
    currency: EUR,
    atlas: (colour: "#226EC7"),
    name_key: "region-continental-europe-maghreb",
    bounds: (west: -16.65, east: 44.95, south: 22.87, north: 59.87),
    grid: (width: 154, height: 123),
